config SPI_PICO_DE_GALLO
	bool "Pico de Gallo SPI controller"
	default y
	depends on DT_HAS_ODP_PICO_DE_GALLO_SPI_ENABLED
	depends on ARCH_POSIX
	select SPI
	help
	  Enable the Pico de Gallo SPI controller driver. This driver forwards
	  Zephyr SPI API calls to a Pico de Gallo USB bridge attached to the host
	  running native_sim via the Pico de Gallo C FFI.

config SPI_PICO_DE_GALLO_INIT_PRIORITY
	int "Pico de Gallo SPI controller initialization priority"
	default 50
	depends on SPI_PICO_DE_GALLO
	help
	  POST_KERNEL initialization priority of the Pico de Gallo SPI
	  controller.

	  It must be greater than CONFIG_GPIO_PICO_DE_GALLO_INIT_PRIORITY
	  (default 45), which must in turn be greater than
	  CONFIG_MFD_PICO_DE_GALLO_INIT_PRIORITY (default 40). This controller
	  configures every pin named in its cs-gpios property as an inactive
	  output at initialization, so the Pico de Gallo GPIO port owning those
	  pins has to be ready first.

	  Kconfig cannot check the arithmetic. Runtime readiness is
	  authoritative instead: an inverted priority makes initialization
	  return -ENODEV before any pin is configured, rather than actuating the
	  wrong line.

config HEAP_MEM_POOL_ADD_SIZE_PDG_SPI
	int "Heap memory pool size for the Pico de Gallo SPI driver"
	default 8192
	depends on SPI_PICO_DE_GALLO
	help
	  pdg_spi_transceive() flattens the caller's scatter-gather buffers into
	  contiguous ones with k_malloc(), one per direction, each at most
	  PDG_SPI_MAX_BUFFER (4096) bytes. A full-size duplex transfer therefore
	  needs about 8 KiB live at once.

	  This has to be declared rather than assumed: k_malloc() lives in
	  kernel/mempool.c, which Zephyr only compiles when the system heap is
	  non-empty, and CONFIG_HEAP_MEM_POOL_SIZE defaults to 0. Without a
	  contribution here the driver fails to link with an undefined reference
	  to k_malloc. The kernel sums every HEAP_MEM_POOL_ADD_SIZE_* symbol and
	  raises the pool to fit, so applications do not have to set
	  CONFIG_HEAP_MEM_POOL_SIZE by hand.

	  Lower this if you know your transfers are small.
